WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.263 --> 00:00:19.524
When Mary Lennox was sent to Misselthwaite Manor to live with her uncle, everyone said she was the

2
00:00:19.564 --> 00:00:21.805
most disagreeable-looking child ever seen.

3
00:00:23.005 --> 00:00:23.866
It was true too.

4
00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:29.067
She had a thin, little face; a thin, little body; and thin, blond hair.

5
00:00:30.207 --> 00:00:34.597
She had a sour look on her face, and her skin was pale because she had always been

6
00:00:34.657 --> 00:00:42.140
sick. She had been born in India, where her father worked for the English government.

7
00:00:43.201 --> 00:00:48.243
Her mother was a great beauty who only wanted to go to parties and amuse herself with interesting

8
00:00:48.303 --> 00:00:51.504
people. She had not wanted a little girl at all.

9
00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:56.867
So when Mary was born, her mother handed her over to the care of a nanny.

10
00:00:57.887 --> 00:01:02.922
The nanny had strict instructions: Keep the baby out of sight as much as possible.

11
00:01:03.942 --> 00:01:08.725
The servants always let Mary do whatever she wanted to keep her from crying and making her mother

12
00:01:08.885 --> 00:01:14.769
angry. By the time Mary was six years old, she was very selfish and stubborn.

13
00:01:15.949 --> 00:01:18.931
A young English governess came to teach her to read and write.

14
00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:23.634
But she disliked Mary so much that she stayed only three months.

15
00:01:24.754 --> 00:01:27.316
Other governesses came and went even faster.

16
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.803
One very hot morning, when she was about ten, Mary awoke feeling grumpy.

17
00:01:34.904 --> 00:01:39.668
She was even grumpier when she saw that the woman standing by her bed was not her usual

18
00:01:39.728 --> 00:01:41.989
nanny. "Why are you here?"

19
00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:43.851
she said to the strange woman.

20
00:01:43.871 --> 00:01:45.612
"I will not let you stay.

21
00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.153
Send my nanny to me."

22
00:01:48.154 --> 00:01:49.355
The woman looked frightened.

23
00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.096
"She cannot come."

24
00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:56.000
Mary flew into a rage and beat and kicked the servant.

25
00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.061
But the frightened woman would only repeat, "The nanny cannot come."

26
00:02:01.081 --> 00:02:07.003
"There is a mystery in the air this morning," said Mary to herself after the servant went away.

27
00:02:08.063 --> 00:02:12.144
As she walked about the house, she noticed that some of the servants were missing.

28
00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:15.145
The ones that she did see looked frightened.

29
00:02:16.706 --> 00:02:20.567
She went out into the garden and began to play under a tree near the porch.

30
00:02:20.587 --> 00:02:24.988
"I can pretend to make a flower garden," said Mary.

31
00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:32.062
She stuck big, red hibiscus blossoms into little heaps of earth, but still felt angry that her nanny

32
00:02:32.082 --> 00:02:32.903
had abandoned her.

33
00:02:34.563 --> 00:02:36.464
Suddenly someone came out on the porch.

34
00:02:37.665 --> 00:02:39.906
It was her mother and a young English soldier.

35
00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:45.148
Her mother's face and clothes were as beautiful as ever, but something was wrong.

36
00:02:46.288 --> 00:02:47.589
Mary's mother looked upset.

37
00:02:47.609 --> 00:02:49.930
"Is it so very bad?

38
00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.050
Oh, is it?"

39
00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:52.551
Mary heard her ask.

40
00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.372
"Awful," said the young soldier.

41
00:02:55.904 --> 00:02:57.845
"You ought to have gone to the hills two weeks ago."

42
00:02:59.406 --> 00:03:01.507
Mary did not know what they were talking about.

43
00:03:02.628 --> 00:03:04.149
She stayed quiet and listened.

44
00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:08.071
"Oh, I know I should have gone," said Mary's mother.

45
00:03:08.091 --> 00:03:11.513
"I only stayed to go to that silly party.

46
00:03:11.973 --> 00:03:13.054
What a fool I was!"

47
00:03:14.214 --> 00:03:17.236
Suddenly the sound of wailing came from the servants' quarters.

48
00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.258
The noise grew louder and wilder.

49
00:03:20.278 --> 00:03:22.559
"What is that?"

50
00:03:22.979 --> 00:03:23.860
cried Mary's mother.

51
00:03:25.052 --> 00:03:27.133
"Someone has died," said the soldier.

52
00:03:27.153 --> 00:03:30.594
"You did not tell me it had broken out among your servants."

53
00:03:30.614 --> 00:03:34.075
"I did not know," said Mary's mother.

54
00:03:34.095 --> 00:03:35.895
"Come with me!"

55
00:03:36.455 --> 00:03:38.596
And she ran into the house with the soldier.

56
00:03:40.216 --> 00:03:42.537
Mary soon learned why the servants were wailing.

57
00:03:43.617 --> 00:03:49.379
Her nanny had died of cholera, a dreaded disease that was spreading quickly and killing many people.

58
00:03:50.339 --> 00:03:55.369
By the next day, three more servants were dead, and the others had run away in terror.

59
00:03:57.151 --> 00:04:03.015
During the confusion of the following day, Mary hid in the nursery and was forgotten by everyone.

60
00:04:04.096 --> 00:04:06.717
Nobody thought of her and nobody wanted her.

61
00:04:07.798 --> 00:04:10.620
Mary alternately cried and slept through the hours.

62
00:04:11.821 --> 00:04:14.343
When she awoke the house was perfectly quiet.

63
00:04:14.363 --> 00:04:18.245
"I wonder if everyone is better," Mary said.

64
00:04:19.806 --> 00:04:25.482
She heard something rustling on the floor, and when she looked down, she saw a little snake gliding

65
00:04:25.562 --> 00:04:29.884
along. "It sounds as if no one is here but the snake and me."

66
00:04:30.965 --> 00:04:34.467
The next minute she heard footsteps on the porch and voices in the house.

67
00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:38.349
Mary jumped out of bed as a soldier came into her room.

68
00:04:38.369 --> 00:04:40.710
"There is a child here!"

69
00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.931
he called to the other soldiers in the house.

70
00:04:42.951 --> 00:04:45.313
"A child alone!

71
00:04:45.753 --> 00:04:46.674
In a place like this!

72
00:04:47.134 --> 00:04:47.654
Who is she?"

73
00:04:48.875 --> 00:04:50.816
"I am Mary Lennox," she said.

74
00:04:51.944 --> 00:04:54.786
"I fell asleep when everyone had cholera, and I just woke up.

75
00:04:55.927 --> 00:04:57.008
Why was I forgotten?

76
00:04:57.428 --> 00:04:58.589
Why does no one come?"

77
00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.651
The soldier looked at her sadly.

78
00:05:01.671 --> 00:05:04.653
"Because there is no one left to come."

79
00:05:06.435 --> 00:05:11.718
So it was in this strange and sudden way that Mary found out that both her father and

80
00:05:11.859 --> 00:05:13.600
mother had died of cholera.

81
00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:19.144
There was no one left in the house but Mary and the little, rustling snake.
